 "pairsdt": {
  "_doc": {
   "outcomes": "BC both correct, YY yes to both orders, NN no to both, BW both wrong; % of images",
   "logor": "pair-matched conditional log-odds log((n_BC+0.5)/(n_BW+0.5)). Under a logistic model P(yes | image i, gold) = sigma(b_i + s * Delta/2) with s = +1 for the order whose gold is 'yes' and -1 for the other, n_BC/n_BW estimates exp(Delta) for any per-image bias b_i (conditional-logit / McNemar MLE), so log-OR = Delta = logit(H_i) - logit(F_i), the per-image logistic sensitivity, free of global, per-image and query-affirming bias (assumes Delta homogeneous over images and the two answers independent given b_i).",
   "dpair_logit": "log-OR / 1.702 (logit(p) ~= 1.702 probit(p)): the per-image d' = z(H_i) - z(F_i) on the probit scale; primary.",
   "dpair_2afc": "sqrt(2) * Phi^-1(BC/(BC+BW)) (2AFC relation); assumes the model compares the two orders' evidence directly; under the yes/no model with bias it is not bias-invariant and overstates d' at small d' (e.g. d' = 1, b = 0 gives 1.37); secondary.",
   "dpooled": "polarity-pooled equal-variance d' (Tab. S24 construction, e17n.json syn.pooled)",
   "ratio_pooled_over_pair": "delta dpooled / delta dpair_logit",
   "acc_decomposition": "two-order accuracy = BC + (YY+NN)/2, so delta acc = -(dYY+dNN)/2 [bias moves] - dBW [reversals]",
   "bootstrap": "2000 resamples of images (paired across arms); seed 21",
   "front_larger_share": 98.6,
   "tercile": "visible-area-ratio terciles (rigor_e17n cut points); YY on high-ratio images = affirming that the smaller, occluded shape is in front when asked (front shape is the larger one in front_larger_share of images); acc_orig_order_delta reproduces the Tab. S22 basis"
  },
